IMPORT prelude

-- Daughters of Charity of the Canossian Institute Incorporation Ordinance 1949 (Singapore) -- who the Corporation "The Mother Superior
-- of the Daughters of Charity of the Canossian Institute (Singapore)" is, including the First Assistant during a vacancy (s 2), what
-- the Ordinance empowers it to do (s 3), which land it vested in the Corporation (s 4 and the Schedule), how its deeds are validly
-- sealed and signed (s 5), what a Gazette notification proves (s 6), and whose rights the Ordinance leaves alone (s 7).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/DCCIIO1949.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The only amendment
-- annotation in the body is "[7/97]" under s 7. The Ordinance is dated 23 November 1949.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0231 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- The Ordinance is seven sections and a Schedule, so the whole of it is in scope. For a person outside the Institute it matters in
-- three places: dealing with the Corporation over property (s 3, s 5), knowing who may act for it when the Mother Superior's office
-- is vacant (s 2(3), s 6), and title to the two scheduled lots at Kallang and Bedok (s 4).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); what "her attorney duly authorised" requires (taken as a stated fact); the "conditions of tenure" and
-- "trusts" subject to which s 4 vests the land; the internal governance of the Society, about which the Ordinance says nothing.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Daughters of Charity of the Canossian Institute Incorporation Ordinance 1949 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2 and 6 -- who is the Corporation, and what the Gazette proves`

-- s 2(1): "The Reverend Vittoria Garré the Mother Superior in the Colony of the Society of the Daughters of Charity of the Canossian
-- Institute and her successors in office, shall be a body corporate (hereinafter called 'the Corporation')", named "The Mother
-- Superior of the Daughters of Charity of the Canossian Institute (Singapore)", with perpetual succession and a corporate seal.
-- s 2(3): "successors in office" is "deemed to include the First Assistant of the Institute from the time when the office ... becomes
-- vacant by the resignation or death of the holder for the time being, until the formal assumption of office by her successor."
-- s 6: a Gazette notification of the appointment of any person to exercise the office "shall be conclusive evidence that such person
-- was duly authorised to exercise the said office in the Colony."
--
-- The deeming in s 2(3) names only two causes of vacancy, resignation and death. A vacancy arising any other way (removal, say) does not
-- bring in the First Assistant on the words; that literal reading is encoded and flagged in NOTES.md. The Gazette proves authorisation
-- only; whether it covers a First Assistant acting under s 2(3) is not said (she is not "appointed").
DECLARE Vacancy IS ONE OF
    `the office is not vacant`
    `vacant by resignation`
    `vacant by death`
    `vacant for another reason`

DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `holds the office of Mother Superior` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the First Assistant of the Institute` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the state of the office` IS A Vacancy
    `a successor has formally assumed office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointment is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the vacancy` IS A Vacancy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a vacancy by resignation or death` IF
    CONSIDER `the vacancy`
    WHEN `vacant by resignation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `vacant by death` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the First Assistant standing in under section 2(3)` IF
        `the claimant`'s `is the First Assistant of the Institute`
    AND `is a vacancy by resignation or death` (`the claimant`'s `the state of the office`)
    AND (NOT `the claimant`'s `a successor has formally assumed office`)

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Corporation's office-holder` IF
        `the claimant`'s `holds the office of Mother Superior`
    OR  `is the First Assistant standing in under section 2(3)` `the claimant`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `authorisation is conclusively proved` IF
    `the claimant`'s `appointment is notified in the Gazette`

§§ `3 -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do`

-- s 2(2): the seal "may from time to time be broken, changed or altered, or made anew as to the Corporation seems fit".
-- s 3(1): the Corporation "may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description, and may sell,
-- convey, assign, exchange, surrender, yield up, mortgage, demise, re-assign, transfer, or otherwise dispose of any movable or immovable
-- property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as to the Corporation seem fit."
-- s 3(2): "The Corporation may sue and be sued in respect of such property in any of the Courts of the Colony of Singapore."
--
-- The powers of disposal reach only property "vested in the Corporation". The capacity to sue and be sued is given "in respect of such
-- property"; the Ordinance grants no other power (whether the general law supplies one is outside the text and not encoded).
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `change or make anew its corporate seal`
    `acquire or purchase property`
    `hold and enjoy property`
    `sell property`
    `exchange property`
    `mortgage property`
    `lease property`
    `transfer or otherwise dispose of property`
    `sue in respect of its property`
    `be sued in respect of its property`
    `sue on a matter not about its property`
    `borrow money without security`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `change or make anew its corporate seal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acquire or purchase property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hold and enjoy property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `exchange property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `mortgage property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `lease property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `transfer or otherwise dispose of property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `sue in respect of its property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `be sued in respect of its property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4 and the Schedule -- the land vested in the Corporation`

-- s 4: the estates and interests of the persons in the third column of the Schedule in the immovable property in the first column "are
-- hereby divested, and the same are vested in the Corporation for the estate or interest indicated in the second column ... subject to
-- all conditions of tenure incident thereto, and subject also to any trusts by which the same are affected."
-- Schedule (1): land in the District of Kallang, 21650.2 square metres, "Lot 1846 of Mukim XXIV", part of Grants Nos. 29, 80, 93 and 58.
-- Schedule (2): land in the District of Bedok, 8498.4 square metres, "Lot 163 of Mukim XXVII", East India Company's Grant No. 63 dated
-- 21 September 1857 made in favour of Punglima Puteh.
--
-- The deposited text of the Schedule table is column-shifted. "Fee simple" appears twice and the third column reads "Vittoria Garré and
-- Bertilia Lim." followed by "Vittoria Garré"; these are matched to items (1) and (2) BY ORDER. That item (2) is fee simple and was
-- held by Vittoria Garré alone is therefore a reading of a shifted table, not something the extracted text shows unambiguously.
-- No other land is vested by s 4: anything else the Corporation holds it holds by acquisition under s 3.
DECLARE Lot IS ONE OF
    `Lot 1846 of Mukim XXIV at Kallang`
    `Lot 163 of Mukim XXVII at Bedok`
    `any other land`

GIVEN `the lot` IS A Lot
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4 vests it in the Corporation` IF
    CONSIDER `the lot`
    WHEN `any other land` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the lot` IS A Lot
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `scheduled area in square metres` IS
    CONSIDER `the lot`
    WHEN `Lot 1846 of Mukim XXIV at Kallang` THEN 21650.2
    WHEN `Lot 163 of Mukim XXVII at Bedok` THEN 8498.4
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `total scheduled area in square metres` IS
        `scheduled area in square metres` `Lot 1846 of Mukim XXIV at Kallang`
    +   `scheduled area in square metres` `Lot 163 of Mukim XXVII at Bedok`

GIVEN `the lot` IS A Lot
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Bertilia Lim's interest is divested` IF
    CONSIDER `the lot`
    WHEN `Lot 1846 of Mukim XXIV at Kallang` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 4 takes the land "subject to all conditions of tenure incident thereto, and subject also to any trusts". A trust or tenure condition
-- that bound the land before vesting still binds it in the Corporation's hands.
GIVEN `the lot` IS A Lot, `the land was subject to a trust before the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation holds it subject to that trust` IF
        `section 4 vests it in the Corporation` `the lot`
    AND `the land was subject to a trust before the Ordinance`

§§ `5 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 5(1): "All deeds and other instruments requiring the seal of the Corporation shall be sealed in the presence of the person who is for
-- the time being Mother Superior in this Colony of the said Society or of her attorney duly authorised and such deeds and instruments and
-- all other documents, instruments and writings requiring the signature of the Corporation shall be signed by such Mother Superior or her
-- attorney."
-- s 5(2): "Such signing shall be and be taken as sufficient evidence that the said seal was duly and properly affixed, and that the seal
-- is the lawful seal of the Corporation."
--
-- The attorney need only be "duly authorised"; s 5 requires no deposit of the power (the Bishop of Singapore Ordinance 1911, s 4(1), as
-- quoted in that Act's naive row, does).
-- s 5 names "the person who is for the time being Mother Superior"; it does not mention the First Assistant who is a "successor in
-- office" under s 2(3). Whether she may seal and sign during a vacancy is not answered by the text. The literal reading -- she may
-- not, unless she is the Mother Superior's attorney -- is encoded and flagged in NOTES.md.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the Mother Superior for the time being`
    `her duly authorised attorney`
    `the First Assistant during a vacancy`
    `a sister with no authority`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Mother Superior or her attorney` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `the Mother Superior for the time being` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `her duly authorised attorney` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is executed as section 5 requires` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the Mother Superior or her attorney` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`)
    AND `is the Mother Superior or her attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence the seal was duly affixed` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the Mother Superior or her attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

§§ `7 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 7: "Nothing in this Ordinance contained shall affect the rights of the Government, all bodies politic and corporate, and all others,
-- except such as are mentioned in this Ordinance and those claiming by, from or under them."
GIVEN `is mentioned in the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims by, from or under a person mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
    `is mentioned in the Ordinance` OR `claims by, from or under a person mentioned`
